# Trivy ignore list: residual poetry.lock advisories that the lock cannot fix
# while the project resolves torch from the pytorch-cu128 index (pyproject.toml
# [[tool.poetry.source]]). Each entry has a reason and an expiry date, using
# Trivy's `exp:` syntax. After that date the advisory fails the scan again, so
# it is re-checked rather than ignored for good.
#
# Every entry below goes away by moving the torch source to the cu129 index,
# which serves torch 2.13.0, or to cu130, which serves 2.14.x. That would also
# lift the setuptools<82 cap and allow a setuptools>=84.1.0 floor. The move
# needs a newer NVIDIA driver on the GPU hosts, so it is a separate decision.

# torch 2.11.0+cu128: fixed in 2.13.0, which the cu128 index does not serve.
CVE-2025-3000 exp:2027-02-09
# The GHSA alias of the CVE above.
GHSA-rrmf-rvhw-rf47 exp:2027-02-09

# setuptools 81.0.0: torch 2.11 declares setuptools<82, and the fix is in 83.0.0.
CVE-2026-59890 exp:2027-02-09
# setuptools 81.0.0: Windows path escape via namespace_packages.txt, fixed in
# 84.1.0 and held back by the same torch cap.
GHSA-xmj3-9gf7-h52w exp:2027-02-09
